OL,3,ASpain's king and queen attend memorial
OL,4,Aservice for rail crash victims
OL,5,
OL,6,FSpain's King Felipe and Queen Letizia
OL,7,Fwere among those who have attended a
OL,8,Fmemorial service in tribute to the 69
OL,9,Fvictims of last month's deadly train
OL,10,Fcrash.
OL,12,FThe accident occurred when one train,
OL,13,Ftravelling at high speed, ploughed into
OL,14,Fthe back of another that was stationary
OL,15,Fon the Madrid-Seville line, near the
OL,16,Fsmall town of Urda, about 40 miles from
OL,17,FToledo.
OL,19,FIt was the worst rail tragedy in Spain
OL,20,Fsince 2013. Twenty-eight people remain
OL,21,Fin hospital.
OL,23,APub: 10-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
